@startuml
title collab Semantic Model — Revised Draft

left to right direction
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam linetype ortho

class Participant {
  +name
  +kind : ParticipantKind
  +multiplicity
}

enum ParticipantKind {
  AO
  HSM
  ISR
  TIMER
}

class Collaboration {
  +isReflexive : Boolean <<derived>>
}

class Route {
  +origin : Participant
  +destination : Participant
}

class EventFlow {
}

class Signal {
  +name
}

abstract class Delivery

class PostDelivery {
  +queueOrder : QueueOrder
}

class PublishSubscribeDelivery
class DispatchDelivery

enum QueueOrder {
  FIFO
  LIFO
}

' Reflexive many-to-many Participant association with Collaboration as association class.
Participant "0..*" -- "0..*" Participant : collaborates with
(Participant, Participant) .. Collaboration

' A collaboration is made concrete by one or more directional routes.
Collaboration "1" *-- "1..*" Route : routes

' Route direction is explicit.
Participant "1" <-- "0..*" Route : origin
Participant "1" <-- "0..*" Route : destination

' One route may carry one or more event flows.
Route "1" *-- "1..*" EventFlow : eventFlows

' Each event flow identifies one signal and one delivery mechanism.
Signal "1" <-- "0..*" EventFlow : signal
Delivery "1" <-- "0..*" EventFlow : delivery

Delivery <|-- PostDelivery
Delivery <|-- PublishSubscribeDelivery
Delivery <|-- DispatchDelivery

PostDelivery --> QueueOrder

note right of Participant
A Participant is a semantic system role/classifier.

Multiplicity records the anticipated runtime
population represented by that participant.
end note

note top of Collaboration
Collaboration is the association class for the
reflexive "collaborates with" relationship.

For participants P1 and P2:
  Collaboration(P1,P2) = Collaboration(P2,P1)

isReflexive is derived:
  true  when P1 = P2
  false when P1 != P2
end note

note bottom of Route
A Route is a directional path from an origin
Participant to a destination Participant.

Therefore:
  Route(P1 -> P2) != Route(P2 -> P1)

A binary Collaboration can contain routes in
either or both directions.

A reflexive Collaboration contains route(s)
whose origin and destination are the same
Participant.
end note

note bottom of EventFlow
An EventFlow is the use of a Signal over a Route
with a particular Delivery mechanism.

The runtime object travelling is an Event;
its Signal identifies the event's semantic type.
end note

note right of Delivery
POST
  queued delivery to an Active Object
  queue order may be FIFO or LIFO

PUBLISH_SUBSCRIBE
  publisher-to-subscriber delivery via QP

DISPATCH
  synchronous delivery to a passive HSM
end note

@enduml
